{
  "_readme": [
    "03-sql/values.json - the ONLY thing the agent writes for the SQL. scripts/render_sql.py builds the four .sql files from it.",
    "Copy this file to RUN_FOLDER/03-sql/values.json and replace every <...>. The renderer refuses any <...>, TODO or TBD left.",
    "Every value is {\"value\": ..., \"source\": ...}. A source names a query ID (Q-...), a 00-inputs.md input, or a decision (decision N = row N of 00-decisions.md).",
    "Numbers may be written as JSON numbers or strings (\"20007.4\"). Keys starting with _ are comments and are ignored.",
    "Steps: every walk step has an entry. status is one of the eight canonical statuses and must equal the step's row in 02-findings.md.",
    "  PROPOSED / DERIVED = build it. SME_DECISION_REQUIRED / EVIDENCE_REQUIRED / EXTERNAL_CHECK_REQUIRED = held (add waits_on); a held step makes the files a DRAFT.",
    "Never write or edit a .sql file. Wrong SQL means wrong values or a template defect: fix values.json, or report the template defect."
  ],
  "run": {
    "run_no": "<run number, e.g. 6>",
    "run_date": "<YYYY-MM-DD>",
    "branch_code": "<e.g. NY_SCH>",
    "target_env": "<e.g. Tier 2 PRE>",
    "env_slug": "<e.g. tier2-pre>"
  },
  "environment": {
